<div class="summary-box">
  <p><strong>We are an independent editorial resource, not a garage, not a dealership, and not affiliated with Jaguar Land Rover Limited.</strong> We research Jaguar engines, publish what we find, and route enquiries to a vetted network of specialists who do the actual work.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>6 published editorial standards</strong> — every piece of content on this site is held to them</li>
    <li><strong>Every number is tagged</strong> to its source — no untagged claims, no invented statistics</li>
    <li><strong>A public corrections log</strong> — when we get something wrong, we say so, openly</li>
    <li><strong>We are paid by specialists for enquiries</strong> — and we disclose that fact plainly, because it's the right thing to do</li>
    <li><strong>We tell people not to replace their engine</strong> when the numbers don't add up — even though it costs us an enquiry</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Full standards, our commercial model, and how we handle corrections, below.</p>
</div>

